      "message": "fix(verify): a raw-stock-only mark dies with the model it was given to\n\nSecond review of PR #1097: the mark named its source by name, so a\nmodel imported under a deleted casting's name inherited it and a real\ngouge posted. DeleteEntity (of the source or the stock), UpdateModel\n(re-import in place) and SetStock (any new stock) now drop the mark in\ntheir own undo step, and undo restores model and mark together; the\nloader reads a mark whose source is missing as unmarked with a note.\nAn empty model no longer counts as something to judge, and the gouge\nhint says what the setting means, shown only for a gouge inside a\nstock source no operation names.\n\nFixes #1094\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
